        ("p", r"<b>A vertical tangent: $f(x) = \sqrt[3]{x}$ at zero.</b> $\frac{\sqrt[3]{\Delta x}}{\Delta x} = \frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{\Delta x^2}} \to +\infty$: the ratio grows without bound, and there is no finite limit."),
