        ("callout", "note", "A subtle example", r"The function $f(x) = x^2\sin\frac1x$ (with $f(0) = 0$) oscillates infinitely often near zero, but by the definition $\frac{f(\Delta x) - 0}{\Delta x} = \Delta x\sin\frac{1}{\Delta x} \to 0$ (a bounded factor times an infinitesimal). So $f'(0) = 0$ exists. The definition is more reliable than intuition “by eye”."),
